<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">raise-zombie</ansi> spell

The <ansi fg="command">Raise Zombie</ansi> spell infuses a corpse with dark vitality,
reanimating it as a shambling undead servant under your command. Zombies
are the workhorse of necromancy — durable, relentless, and easily created
from the remains of common creatures.

Zombies are hardy and methodical, using brute strength in melee combat. They
move with ponderous, remorseless steps and can withstand considerable damage.

The undead servant's power scales with your willpower and spellcasting skill.
More skilled casters raise more formidable specimens.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cast raise-zombie [corpse]</ansi>     Animate nearby remains.

<ansi fg="yellow">Base Folds:  </ansi> Brief channel
<ansi fg="yellow">Corpse:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Requires modest remains</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Target:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Nearby corpse or ground loot</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Conv. Cost:  </ansi> Moderate
<ansi fg="yellow">School:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Manifestation</ansi>

<ansi fg="white-bold">Notes:</ansi>
  - The zombie appears under your command and aids you in combat.
  - Once raised, the undead servant remains active as a companion.
  - Use the <ansi fg="command">assess</ansi> command to evaluate a corpse's quality.

